{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review remediation round 1 (BLOCK -> remediated):\n- COH/E1: AC1's 'byte-unchanged' conflated two claims. Clarified: stored code-v3 sidecars are never rewritten/re-scored in place (version-gated; the 42->99 replay is offline analysis, not a migration); the new binary contributes 0 when absent.\n- G6 (real forward hazard): the lane-blind reversibility floor could lift a minor debt binary on a hard_to_reverse surface to 0.6 and cross tests@0.54. v4 now restricts the floor to the consequence lanes (consequence base>0 AND hard_to_reverse_surface); debt never floors. Corpus-verified: replay identical (163/99); 4 existing debt-only+hard-to-reverse findings stay advisory; unit test added to Testing.\n- T8: prod_impact/trigger_likelihood are documented production-scoped; plan now amends both field descriptions (code-review-verify.md + verify_models.py) to state the maintainability user-reach keying. Corpus crosstab shows verifiers already answer them this way for maint findings, so this documents existing behavior rather than shifting the distribution the replay was grounded on."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787192982875220001,"uuid":"448d11cf-e1d0-4515-88e6-aede6af00192"}